383 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (AugDiff leverages generative models \(Variational Autoencoders, U-Net, and diffusion models\) to create realistic and diverse synthetic features directly in the learned feature space. During augmentation, random noise is added to latent rapresentation of feature vectors, and the autoencoder denoises them to generate new synthetic samples that remain semantically consistent with the original tissue representation.  Compared to traditional augmentation methods, is particularly effective at maintaining the biological meaning of the features, supporting online augmentation during model training, and improving robustness and generalization.)
/E (AugDiff leverages generative models \(Variational Autoencoders, U-Net, and diffusion models\) to create realistic and diverse synthetic features directly in the learned feature space. During augmentation, random noise is added to latent rapresentation of feature vectors, and the autoencoder denoises them to generate new synthetic samples that remain semantically consistent with the original tissue representation.  Compared to traditional augmentation methods, is particularly effective at maintaining the biological meaning of the features, supporting online augmentation during model training, and improving robustness and generalization.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
